1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,503
Someone on your site just spotted a hazard.

2
00:00:02,503 --> 00:00:05,680
What happens next decides whether it gets fixed, or forgotten.

3
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:08,903
This is the complete SafeWorks walkthrough:

4
00:00:08,903 --> 00:00:13,279
the phone app, the QR form for visitors, the admin console, and the settings that

5
00:00:13,279 --> 00:00:14,630
shape how your sites run.

6
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:20,229
Sign in with your employee code or email, in English, Hindi, Tamil or Kannada.

7
00:00:20,229 --> 00:00:22,759
New workers use a one-time enrolment code;

8
00:00:22,759 --> 00:00:25,410
managers add a six-digit authenticator code.

9
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:30,612
Home shows your sync status, the Report button, and what needs you now:

10
00:00:30,612 --> 00:00:35,702
overdue actions, items to verify, triage backlog and inspections due, then this week

11
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:36,490
at your site.

12
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:40,133
Quick report has every option on one screen:

13
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:45,309
location from GPS or the QR poster, type, categories, up to ten photos, a spoken or

14
00:00:45,309 --> 00:00:47,615
typed description, then the switches:

15
00:00:47,615 --> 00:00:50,733
fixed on the spot, danger now, report anonymously.

16
00:00:50,733 --> 00:00:53,040
More details adds employer and trade.

17
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:55,348
Reports has three tabs:

18
00:00:55,348 --> 00:00:57,920
My reports, Triage for officers, and Site.

19
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:02,880
Search, save a filter, and open any report for its photos, timeline, comments and

20
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:03,370
actions.

21
00:01:04,270 --> 00:01:06,006
Triage offers seven decisions:

22
00:01:06,006 --> 00:01:10,519
accept and assign, fixed on the spot, return with a question, reviewed, merge,

23
00:01:10,519 --> 00:01:12,603
discard, or escalate to an incident.

24
00:01:12,603 --> 00:01:17,463
Accept and assign scores the risk on the matrix, asks for an interim control on high

25
00:01:17,463 --> 00:01:20,530
risks, and creates actions with owners and due dates.

26
00:01:21,430 --> 00:01:23,652
Owners see their actions, overdue first.

27
00:01:23,652 --> 00:01:27,485
Start the work, then Complete with an after-photo and the root cause.

28
00:01:27,485 --> 00:01:30,707
Request a new date, or dispute an action that isn't yours;

29
00:01:30,707 --> 00:01:33,040
reminders pause while the officer decides.

30
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:39,743
A verifier, never the owner, compares before and after and marks the fix effective

31
00:01:39,743 --> 00:01:40,142
or not.

32
00:01:40,142 --> 00:01:44,360
When every action is verified, the report closes and the reporter is told.

33
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:49,687
Danger now sends a stop-work alert to the officers, site head and HSE managers.

34
00:01:49,687 --> 00:01:53,330
They must acknowledge it within the target time, or it escalates.

35
00:01:54,230 --> 00:01:54,866
No signal?

36
00:01:54,866 --> 00:01:59,573
Everything waits in the Outbox and sends itself when you're back in range.

37
00:01:59,573 --> 00:02:04,217
Sync now, retry failed items, fix and resend a rejected report, or export

38
00:02:04,217 --> 00:02:04,980
diagnostics.

39
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:10,527
Visitors and contract workers scan the QR poster, pick a language, report in a few

40
00:02:10,527 --> 00:02:14,890
taps, stay anonymous if they wish, and get a private link to follow progress.

41
00:02:15,790 --> 00:02:18,687
Inspections run from a template or a schedule:

42
00:02:18,687 --> 00:02:22,024
pass, fail or N A, numbers, choices, text and photos.

43
00:02:22,024 --> 00:02:25,992
A failed item asks for a photo, a note and a corrective action.

44
00:02:25,992 --> 00:02:26,936
Sign on screen;

45
00:02:26,936 --> 00:02:28,070
the run is scored.

46
00:02:28,970 --> 00:02:33,544
Charts show your own numbers, your department's, or the whole site, over thirty,

47
00:02:33,544 --> 00:02:35,373
ninety or three sixty five days.

48
00:02:35,373 --> 00:02:37,660
Officers download the full Excel report.

49
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:42,184
Notifications collect alerts, reminders and closure notices.

50
00:02:42,184 --> 00:02:47,197
Settings holds your language, appearance, email digest, quiet hours and the privacy

51
00:02:47,197 --> 00:02:47,620
notice.

52
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:50,983
The admin console opens on the dashboard:

53
00:02:50,983 --> 00:02:55,369
open and overdue actions, triage backlog, on-time closure, participation,

54
00:02:55,369 --> 00:03:00,055
acknowledgement time, inspection completion, repeat findings and percent safe.

55
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:01,557
Filter by site and dates;

56
00:03:01,557 --> 00:03:03,660
export the view or the full report.

57
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:07,534
The attention board lists what needs someone today:

58
00:03:07,534 --> 00:03:12,374
triage, unacknowledged alerts, overdue actions, missed inspections, repeat findings

59
00:03:12,374 --> 00:03:13,540
and health warnings.

60
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:19,468
The registers list every observation, action and inspection, with filters for

61
00:03:19,468 --> 00:03:22,668
status, risk, type, category, employer and dates.

62
00:03:22,668 --> 00:03:27,370
Save a filter, open the side panel, jump to a case, export CSV or Excel.

63
00:03:28,270 --> 00:03:30,428
Press Control K for the command menu:

64
00:03:30,428 --> 00:03:33,810
type a page name, or paste a case number, and press Enter.

65
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:35,742
Sites and areas:

66
00:03:35,742 --> 00:03:41,097
the wizard creates a site by industry with default areas, templates, categories and

67
00:03:41,097 --> 00:03:41,807
QR posters.

68
00:03:41,807 --> 00:03:46,194
Each site holds its rule set, matrix version, calendar and geofence.

69
00:03:46,194 --> 00:03:48,323
Equipment is registered per area;

70
00:03:48,323 --> 00:03:50,130
QR codes rotate and reprint.

71
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:55,477
People and contractors hold workers without a login, contractor companies with their

72
00:03:55,477 --> 00:03:58,600
trades and sites, and the department list, with CSV import.

73
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,463
Users and roles:

74
00:04:00,463 --> 00:04:05,518
each person signs in with an employee code, email or enrolment code, and holds roles

75
00:04:05,518 --> 00:04:07,022
per site or company wide.

76
00:04:07,022 --> 00:04:11,957
Issue enrolment codes, reset passwords and authenticators, unlock accounts, set an

77
00:04:11,957 --> 00:04:12,980
auditor's expiry.

78
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:18,088
Categories carry required fields, recipients and whether they can be critical.

79
00:04:18,088 --> 00:04:19,652
The risk matrix is versioned.

80
00:04:19,652 --> 00:04:23,428
Due dates and reminders set the days per band and the reminder ladder.

81
00:04:23,428 --> 00:04:25,370
Rule sets hold the statutory timers.

82
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:30,708
The template builder has sections, eight question types, guidance, action on fail

83
00:04:30,708 --> 00:04:33,009
and pass marks, with a live phone preview;

84
00:04:33,009 --> 00:04:35,092
a second person approves each version.

85
00:04:35,092 --> 00:04:38,160
Schedules make inspections recur for a person or a role.

86
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:41,906
Languages shows how complete each translation is.

87
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:46,495
Settings holds the company identity, two-step sign-in roles, languages, service

88
00:04:46,495 --> 00:04:49,980
levels, quiet hours, push cap, duplicates and photo quality.

89
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:51,459
Oversight:

90
00:04:51,459 --> 00:04:55,628
the audit log records every change with a chain you verify in one click;

91
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:58,117
the notifications log shows every delivery;

92
00:04:58,117 --> 00:05:01,070
Health, Privacy and Retention complete the picture.

93
00:05:01,970 --> 00:05:02,935
That's SafeWorks:

94
00:05:02,935 --> 00:05:07,706
reports in seconds, fixes that are owned and verified, inspections with proof, and a

95
00:05:07,706 --> 00:05:09,750
console that gives managers control.

96
00:05:10,650 --> 00:05:14,916
Choose your pilot site, print your posters, and make your first report today.

97
00:05:14,916 --> 00:05:16,080
Welcome to SafeWorks.
